GENERIC_GUIDANCE='''For coding tasks, identify the required behavior and compatibility constraints before editing. Inspect relevant files with Read, Glob and Grep. Prefer Edit for targeted source changes and Write for new files or complete replacements. Avoid nested Bash/python -c strings and shell heredocs for modifying source; if a helper script is necessary, create it with Write and run the file. Use Bash for running tests and other authorized commands. After an error, inspect its actual output and change the diagnosis or action instead of repeating the same failed command unchanged. Check each requested behavior, including filtering and edge cases, against tests. Preserve existing public interfaces unless the user requests a change. Run the relevant test suite and report actual failures honestly; do not claim completion while required checks fail. Follow the user's scope and tool permissions.'''
WINDOWS_GUIDANCE='''Local Windows coding environment: Bash already starts in the selected project directory. Use the Python command python, not python3. Do not probe /tmp, /usr/bin or Unix interpreter locations. Run tests as a standalone command such as python -m unittest discover; do not prepend cd or chain unrelated shell commands. Use Glob to find the real project files, then Read them; do not guess a src/ layout. Use Edit for targeted code changes and Write for new files or complete replacements. Avoid modifying code through nested python -c strings or shell heredocs; create a helper with Write if necessary, then run python helper.py. Read error output and change the failing action instead of repeating it unchanged. Check every requested behavior and compatibility requirement, including filters and rounding. Run the test suite and report actual results honestly. Respect the user's scope, protected files and tool permissions.'''
